{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgS9cWz9MSeWzA2tRYgyL","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"A new memory no longer forces the static instructions to be re-written. A `save_fact` now only re-writes the small facts block (tens of tokens instead of ~1100). I tested this with a fake client, not the real API, so the token savings are still estimates.\n\n**Cause:** the coaching rules and the athlete's facts were one system block with one cache marker. Caching only reuses a prompt up to a marker if nothing before it has changed, so adding one fact made the whole prompt get written again. The prompt was also rebuilt on every tool round, so the miss landed on round 2 of the same message. That is the \"call right after a save_fact\" in `logs/usage.jsonl`.\n\n**Changes in `bot.py`:**\n1. **System prompt split into three blocks**, each with its own cache marker: the coaching rules (the same for every athlete), the athlete profile (name, zones, goal, language), and the long-term facts plus today's date. A new fact only changes the last block. Moving the date there also means midnight no longer evicts the rules.\n2. **Prompt built once per message** instead of once per tool round. The model already sees the new fact in its own tool call, and the fact appears in the prompt from the next message on.\n3. **Longer descriptions for `save_fact` and `log_session`.** Sonnet 4.5 only caches a prompt prefix of at least 1024 tokens, and below that it skips caching without any error. The logs show Jonas's whole prompt was exactly 1024 tokens, which puts tools + rules at about 930. Splitting the blocks alone would therefore have cached nothing static. The new descriptions add roughly 190 tokens and give the model clearer guidance on when to save a fact or log a session.\n4. **Warning on stderr** when a call neither reads nor writes cache, so dropping back under the minimum after a future trim won't go unnoticed.\n\nThe keyword-based tool filtering is unchanged, as `NOTES.md` asks. I also updated the caching sentence in `README.md`, and `ANSWER.md` has the full write-up.\n\n**Tested:** a fake client confirmed that the prompt stays the same within a message and that only the facts block changes after `save_fact`.\n\n**Not tested:** I made no real API calls, so the ~1100-token size of tools + rules is estimated from character counts. To confirm, send a few messages including one that saves a fact. The call after the fact should show about 1100+ in `cache_read_input_tokens` and only a small `cache_creation_input_tokens`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":98,"cache_read_input_tokens":45194,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":98},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3002ca77-651b-4040-9a97-3966141a3e9f","uuid":"f597d424-7577-4373-a74f-ec7a262be38b","timestamp":"2026-10-27T04:57:48.618Z","request_id":"req_011CgS9cWkWNZT7TxKK47mgv"}
